A||||8||Black88GT||'88 Shocks, problemo||||5||
Z||000000||Black88GT||05-15-2001||12:29 AM||||I went out to do my shocks and front swaybar bushings hoping to cure my everlasting squeeking problem.  Well after breaking both of the sway bar bushing "shafts" (I guess thats what they call them) and spending an hour on each side to get them off, I finally made it to the shocks.  Well, I can't get that top nut off.  Everytime I try to turn it the whole thing turns, but there's nothing to hold it with.  It looks like the top might be shaped for some kind of socket but I can't tell which kind.  Do I need a special socket for it or something?  I hope not. I need to have this done ASAP.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-15-2001||01:18 AM||||The top nut is 15mm, but if the old shocks are more than a few years old this nut won't come off easily.  Put the box end on the nut and then clamp a pair of vice grips to the top of the shaft and try turning the nut......sometimes this works.  You will more than likely have to cut the nut off.<P>Go to your auto parts store and buy a "nut breaker"....it'll be around $8-$10, but is well worth the investment.  What this does is break the nut in half allowing removal of the shock.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||05-15-2001||05:21 PM||||Hehe, I was going to email you Mike but I would think your tired of all my emails recently! lol.  I am getting that tool tomorrow, there are a few variations on the theme though, "nut cracker", "nut splitter", and my personal fav., "nut buster".  <P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||fiero56||05-15-2001||05:28 PM||||I had the same problem, a nut splitter fixed the problem. Also, I had a very annoying squeak, couldn't track it down, turned out the post near the top shock mount was terribly rusted away, and was squeaking. New shocks fixed the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||05-16-2001||12:09 AM||||yeah thats why I am trying the shocks since someone, might have been you actually, said the same thing on my other post about squeeking.  <P>Well I will take a crack at it tomorrow.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||sjp777||05-16-2001||12:16 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>yeah thats why I am trying the shocks since someone, might have been you actually, said the same thing on my other post about squeeking.  <P>Well I will take a crack at it tomorrow.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, that was me. I had the same prob when I replaced the front shocks. The nut splitter is about the only solution. New shocks come with new nuts, so tear em up.<P>Another thing you might want to try: I replaced the top rubber bushing on the shock with a leftover urethane bushing from when I put new swaybar endlinks on. Fits perfect.<P><BR>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><P>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-16-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Coop88||05-16-2001||04:52 AM||||If you're gonna replace the shocks anyway, just unbolt the shock at the bottom, so it will extend fully. Then take a pair of vice-grips and clamp down on the shaft, going through the spring. Works for me. If you wanna save the shocks, use the 'nut buster'.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TRL46202||05-16-2001||08:50 AM||||Place your ratchet over the nut and bend it back and forth. The shaft is very thin and will snap right off. You don't need the old shock anyway.<P>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||05-16-2001||09:50 PM||||Whew I got them off with that nut splitter or breaker whatever its called.  Finished both sides in about 20 min.  Now I just need to get the pass. side sway bar thing off after that broke too and I will be done.<P>If it squeeks after this I think I am going to drive it off a cliff with me in it!!!<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
